\u001b[83Geans\u001b[88Git\u001b[91Gsigns\u001b[97Gpuzzles\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gwith TYPO3's encryption key,\u001b[34Gwhich is\u001b[43Gf\u001b[45Gne, and th\u001b[56G change\u001b[64Gbelongs\u001b[72Gin\u001b[75Gthe\u001b[79Gcommit.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mREADME:\u001b[13G\u001b[22ma\u001b[15Gsection\u001b[23Gon\u001b[26GALTCHA.\u001b[34G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdata.xml\u001b[43G\u001b[39mdidn't\u001b[50Gchange.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mThing\u001b[10Gyou should know:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mIt's a hurdle, not a wall.\u001b[22m It stops bots that don't \u001b[58Gun JavaScript or d\u001b[78G't solve ALTCHA puzzles.\u001b[103GA\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Betermined\u001b[16Gspamm\u001b[22Gr can\u001b[29Gtill solve it cheaply: my script needed\u001b[69G0.1 sec\u001b[77Gnds. You can raise the\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gdifficulty in the site settings\u001b[37G(\u001b[38;2;177;185;249maltcha.maximumComplexity\u001b[39m),\u001b[65Gbut that slow\u001b[79G dow\u001b[84G cheap phon\u001b[96Gs \u001b[99Goo.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mCleanup needs a cron job.\u001b[22m Every page view s\u001b[49Gore\u001b[53G one puzzle in the database, and \u001b[87Gothing deletes them\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bautomatically. The scheduler extension isn't installed, so production needs a cron\u001b[88Gjob\u001b[92Grunning\u001b[100G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mtypo3 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[5G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249maltcha:remove-obsolete-challenges --include-solved-challenges\u001b[39m. It'\u001b[72G in the README.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mReady for TYPO3 14.3 but not 15.\u001b[22m Th\u001b[69Gm s\u001b[73Gtup the old TypoScript way, which\u001b[31;1H\u001b[29;3H\u001b[?25h"]
