[1430.236905, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[5G\u001b[1mContent filter\u001b[22m, e.g. reject\u001b[39GTakes away the\u001b[59G     \u001b[65G   \u001b[69G       \u001b[77G      \u001b[84G    \u001b[89G        \u001b[98G  \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bmessages\u001b[14Gwith\u001b[19Glinks    \u001b[39Gpayoff of link\u001b[54G  \u001b[59GAlso blocks citizens who pa\u001b[87Gt\u001b[89G a link     \r\u001b[38C\u001b[1Bspam   \u001b[59G    \r\u001b[4C\u001b[2B               \u001b[21G    \u001b[26G      \u001b[40Ghe mail serv\u001b[53Gr\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mMail rules at the municipality\u001b[39G\u001b[22mor a \u001b[45Gilter sorts\u001b[59GNot in TYPO3; \u001b[74Ghe municipali\u001b[88Gy's\u001b[92GIT does\u001b[100Git\r\u001b[38C\u001b[1B the\u001b[44Gmessages\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B└\u001b[37G┴\u001b[57G┴\u001b[103G┘\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mMy recommendation\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BKeep the honeypot and ALTCHA as they are. Together they stop untargeted bots, which is the spam a\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmunicipal\u001b[13Gcontact\u001b[21Gform\u001b[26Gactually\u001b[35Ggets,\u001b[41Gwithout\u001b[49Gbothering\u001b[59Gvisitors.\u001b[69GRaising\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81Gdifficulty\u001b[92Gmostly\u001b[99Ghurts\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bvisitors on slow phones.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BIf the site gets t\u001b[22Grgeted floods later, the n\u001b[49Gxt step is a \u001b[63Ger-IP limit, not a \u001b[83Garder puzzle. TYPO3\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Balready has a built-in\u001b[26Gra\u001b[29Ge \u001b[32Gimit\u001b[37Gr, the one the backend login uses, and a small validator in the\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bs\u001b[5Gtepackage\u001b[15Gcould use it.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BDo\u001b[6Gyou\u001b[10Gwant\u001b[15Gm\u001b[17G to build the per-IP limit now, or\u001b[52Gwait\u001b[57Guntil spam actually shows up?\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GBaked for 21s · done 6:54 PM\r\u001b[2B\u001