[1441.245192, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[1mMy recommendation\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BKeep the honeypot and ALTCHA as they are. Together they stop untargeted bots, which is the spam a\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmunicipal\u001b[13Gcontact\u001b[21Gform\u001b[26Gactually\u001b[35Ggets,\u001b[41Gwithout\u001b[49Gbothering\u001b[59Gvisitors.\u001b[69GRaising\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81Gdifficulty\u001b[92Gmostly\u001b[99Ghurts\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bvisitors on slow phones.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BIf the site gets t\u001b[22Grgeted floods later, the n\u001b[49Gxt step is a \u001b[63Ger-IP limit, not a \u001b[83Garder puzzle. TYPO3\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Balready has a built-in\u001b[26Gra\u001b[29Ge \u001b[32Gimit\u001b[37Gr, the one the backend login uses, and a small validator in the\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bs\u001b[5Gtepackage\u001b[15Gcould use it.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BDo\u001b[6Gyou\u001b[10Gwant\u001b[15Gm\u001b[17G to build the per-IP limit now, or\u001b[52Gwait\u001b[57Guntil spam actually shows up?\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GBaked for 21s · done 6:54 PM\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mwhere is the personal data of the senders saved?\u001b[39m                                                        \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'll check this against the installation\u001b[44Grather\u001b[51Gthan\u001b[56Ganswer\u001b[63Gfrom\u001b[68Gmemory.\u001b[76GSearching\u001b[86Gthe\u001b[90Gwhole\u001b[96Gdatabase,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe\u001b[7GTYPO3\u001b[13Glogs\u001b[18Gand\u001b[22Gthe\u001b[26Gweb\u001b[30Gserver\u001b[37Glogs\u001b[42Gfor\u001b[46Gthe\u001b[50Gtest\u001b[55Gsender's\u001b[64Gdata:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning\u001b[11G\u001b[1m1\u001b[13G\u001b[22mshell\u001b[19Gcommand…\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ ddev exec \"mysqldump -udb -pdb db 2>/de